cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this artifact, please cite the associated paper:
  "Who Saw It First: Zero-Day Propagation and Attribution Leakage in Federated Intrusion Detection".
title: "Who Saw It First: Zero-Day Propagation and Attribution Leakage in Federated Intrusion Detection — Reproducibility Artifact"
abstract: >-
  Artifact package for the IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy (S&P) paper
  "Who Saw It First: Zero-Day Propagation and Attribution Leakage in Federated Intrusion Detection".
  Contains cross-silo federated learning simulation harnesses, shadow-federation
  meta-classifiers, defensive evaluations (SecAgg, Client DP, Quorum Escrow),
  machine-checked Lean 4 formal proofs for all 9 theoretical results, preprocessed
  intrusion detection benchmarks, and automated verification tooling.
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous"
    affiliation: "Redacted for double-blind peer review"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://anonymous.4open.science/r/FedLearn-CDE3/"
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - network intrusion detection
  - privacy leakage
  - origin attribution
  - zero-day attacks
  - secure aggregation
  - formal verification
  - lean 4

